(7) utilize passage of a recognized national exam such as the NCCPA PANCE as a
requirement for PA licensure; and
(8) grant the compact privilege to a holder of a qualifying license in a participating state.
(b) Nothing in this compact shall prohibit a participating state from charging a fee for
granting the compact privilege.
